- ### Text that is not one word
+ ### Texto que no es una sola palabra

- Hyphenation applies to letters, and text is rarely only letters. Each run of letters is
- hyphenated independently. Everything else, such as spaces, punctuation and digits, passes
- through untouched:
+ La separación silábica se aplica a las letras, y el texto rara vez es solo letras. Cada racha de
+ letras se divide de forma independiente. Todo lo demás, como los espacios, la puntuación y los
+ dígitos, pasa intacto:

= through untouched:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= through untouched:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= through untouched:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(t"hello, world!".hyphenate(hyphen = '-'))
+ Out.println(t"hello, world!".hyphenate(hyphen = '-'))

- Out.println(t"the algorithm runs".hyphenate(hyphen = '-'))
+ Out.println(t"the algorithm runs".hyphenate(hyphen = '-'))

= Out.println(t"the algorithm runs".hyphenate(hyphen = '-'))
- ```
+ ```

- Both words of the first text are too short to break. `syllables` follows the same rule, and
- gives the runs which are not letters as segments of their own, so putting the segments back
- together reproduces the original text exactly.
+ Las dos palabras del primer texto son demasiado cortas para partirse. `syllables` sigue la misma
+ regla, y da las rachas que no son letras como segmentos propios, de modo que volver a juntar los
+ segmentos reproduce exactamente el texto original.

- ### Extending the patterns
+ ### Ampliar los patrones

- A word from a specialist field, which the standard patterns break wrongly, or not at all,
- is taught with an extra pattern, in TeX's notation, layered over the existing set:
+ A una palabra de un campo especializado, que los patrones estándar parten mal, o no parten en
+ absoluto, se le enseña con un patrón adicional, en la notación de TeX, superpuesto al conjunto
+ existente:

= is taught with an extra pattern, in TeX's notation, layered over the existing set:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= is taught with an extra pattern, in TeX's notation, layered over the existing set:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= is taught with an extra pattern, in TeX's notation, layered over the existing set:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
